<title>JAPAN: NCB shares edge higher on buying back.</title>
<headline>NCB shares edge higher on buying back.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Credit Bank Ltd shares edged higher on Tuesday afternoon as buying back emerged following relentless selling in past sessions, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0455 GMT, the shares were up 10 yen at 171. There were 9.76 million shares traded, making NCB the most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
